Install PE_halt_restart + a safety WDT before IOKit (covers SMP bring-up).

0137 installs the platform reset hook only in onc_emmc_init(), which runs after
SweetCPU::startAll().  Every panic before that (e.g. the current
"SWEET CPU: cpu=1 startup timeout") leaves the phone spinning on the panic
screen, so each SMP iteration needs a manual long-press.

0143 (2 files, no functional change to the 0137 later path):

  osfmk/arm/arm_init.c
    - call sweet_early_reset_install() right after PE_init_cpu() on the boot
      CPU (VM is up after arm_vm_init, console is up after PE_init_printf,
      ml_io_map works, and it is still before IOKit / SweetCPU::startAll).
      Guarded by `#if defined(SWEET) && defined(ONC_SWEET_4K)`.

  bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
    - `sweet_early_reset_install()` (global): `sweetearlyreset=0` disables;
      otherwise map the KPSS WDT page, install
      PE_halt_restart = sweet_pe_halt_restart (0137 hook: PSCI attempt then
      WDT bite, never returns) and arm a safety watchdog for 120 s
      (`sweetearlywdts=<secs>` override, clamped to 600).
      Banner: "SWEET RESET: early hook install, safety WDT N s".
    - `sweet_wdt_disarm()`: EN=0; dsb; RST=1; dsb (+ STS readback).
    - onc_emmc_init(): the 0137 assignment becomes idempotent
      ("PE_halt_restart already hooked early") and the safety WDT is disarmed
      here, because from now on the hook covers panics and a live boot must
      not bite.  With `sweetearlyreset=0` the original 0137 install path is
      still taken, exactly as before.
    - Nothing else changes; sweetrebootat's pre-shutdown WDT arm is untouched.

Why this point: arm_init() runs after arm_vm_init() (vm map alive) and after
PE_init_printf() (kprintf works), so ml_io_map(0x0b017000) and the hook's
printf/MMIO reset are safe there; it is before machine_startup() and therefore
before IOKit matching and SweetCPU::startAll().  A panic/hang between
PE_init_cpu() and onc_emmc_init() now resets via the hook (panic) or the
120 s safety WDT (hang).

Expected new console lines:
  SWEET RESET: early hook install, safety WDT 120 s
  SWEET WDT: armed bite in 3932160 ticks
  SWEET WDT: bite (STS=0x...)
  ...normal boot...
  SWEET HALT: PE_halt_restart already hooked early
  SWEET WDT: safety WDT disarmed (STS=0x...)
and on an early panic:
  SWEET HALT: type=%u -> WDT reset
  SWEET RESET: PSCI SYSTEM_RESET
  SWEET RESET: PSCI returned 0xffffffffffffffff, falling back to watchdog
  SWEET WDT: armed bite in 8192 ticks
  SWEET WDT: bite (STS=0x...)
